.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH delete 1  "delete " 
.SH NAME
delete \- Mark sessions deleted on the remote (encrypted bytes stay in the pack, the local file stays)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdelete\fR [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISESSIONS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark a session deleted on the remote and drop its index entry. The encrypted bytes stay in the remote pack
gist until a prune, which is not part of sync yet.
.PP
The local file is never touched. The delete applies to the newest version of the session at the
time it runs, a version another machine pushed since the preview is deleted too. Patterns use * (any run) and ? (one character) against
<agent>/<name> of the remote sessions. More than 10 matches ask to type the count.
When nothing matches it prints Nothing to delete. and exits 0.
.PP
EXAMPLE:
    agr sync delete claude/a.cast.gz
    agr sync delete \*(Aqclaude/2024\-*\*(Aq
    agr sync delete \-\-all \-\-dry\-run
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Delete every remote session
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Allow more than 10 deletes without a terminal, a terminal still asks the count
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would happen, change nothing
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip the confirmation prompt
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
List every session, not only the summary
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fISESSIONS\fR]
Patterns with * and ?, e.g. claude/*
